;; NAMES-ONLY snapshot of the NIST v2-validation engine's own finding
;; vocabulary (pairing-as-data, ADR-0088, AR-PD-3): every `classification`
;; and `category` display name `reference.conf` (packaged inside the
;; resolved gov.nist:hl7-v2-validation jar) declares, and nothing else --
;; no template text, no per-detection config bodies. The `notice_verbatim`
;; discipline (.agents/rulings.md, vendoring arc) applied to a vocabulary
;; rather than a byte-for-byte artifact: this file is factual reference,
;; re-derived from the SAME resolved jar on every test run
;; (components/judge-v2-nist/test/ehrt/judge_v2_nist/taxonomy_currency_test.clj)
;; and the test fails on drift -- a version bump that adds, removes, or
;; renames a classification or category breaks this gate rather than
;; silently going stale.
;;
;; :engine records the jar version this snapshot was actually measured
;; against (its own pom.properties-derived version, same provenance
;; discipline docs/engine-onboarding.md names for every other engine
;; measurement in this repo).
;;
;; Keys are reference.conf's own HOCON path segments (e.g. "r-usage"'s
;; own `category = ${report.category.usage}` resolves the "usage" key
;; below to display name "Usage"); values are the display-name strings
;; that actually appear on a live Report Entry's own .getCategory()/
;; .getClassification() -- ehrt.judge.pairing registry rows whose :judge
;; is :judge-v2-nist draw every :expected member from this file's own
;; :categories values (schema-checked by the currency test above, not by
;; ehrt.judge.pairing itself -- see that namespace's own docstring for
;; why the check lives at the test-tier boundary instead).
{:engine {:name "nist-v2-validation" :version "1.7.3"}

